Z||000005||TheFiero64||10-11-2000||07:05 PM||||I just sent this to Hot Rod.<BR>I was just talking with a fellow Fiero owner Phil Randolph. I was looking forward to seeing a 3 page color article that was going to be in the December issue. Fieros are one of the most popular cars out there right now on the car show and hotrod circuit. There are more Fiero clubs out there than almost any other class of car. I belong to a Fiero forum with almost 4000 members. If you were to start featuring more Fieros in your pages I bet you could make your number of subscriptions grow. I know I joined the ranks after seeing a Fiero article a wile ago. <P>if anyone else feels like writing in here is the hyperlink <A HREF="http://www.hotrodarchives.com/corporatePages/usercomments.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.hotrodarchives.com/corporatePages/usercomments.htm</A> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Old Lar||10-11-2000||07:44 PM||||What can I say.. I feel your pain...naa too Clintonesque.  Those that have seen your 3800 s/c know what a nice ride you have.  I for one, am envious of the cross country power tours that you have been taking.  I can always post a few more Phil's photos on the forum that I have on file.  The article may pop up when you least expect it.  Maybe you can send a story and photo to "High Performance Pontiac".  The last page has an article on my favorite ride or something like that.  You car would fit right in.<P>You just have to get a photo of the car with all the trophys you've won..Remember John Deer.  But I'm an international winner now, having got a 3rd place in the GTA show in Sept.  I'll add that to my resume.  BFD  Mine goes off the road soon..winter is approaching.<P>See you in Daytona in March?||||reg||6
